<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Omride dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 885–841 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a> · Also known as House of Omri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Omride dynasty was the royal house of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a> around 885 BCE and destroyed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>'s coup around 841 BCE. Under Omri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahab">Ahab</a> Israel became a significant regional power, building <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a> as its capital, allying with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicia">Phoenicia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> and ruling Moab. Assyrian texts went on calling Israel the 'House of Omri' long after the dynasty fell.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omride-dynasty.jpg" alt="Omride dynasty" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bukvoed · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sebastia-393.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
